@startuml dual-metering
!include _theme.puml
title Indevolt dual metering — three app data sources
left to right direction

component "Atmoce PV\nMC100 · 9 kWp" as pv <<pv>>
component "Home Assistant" as ha <<ha>>
component "Simulated Shelly 3EM" as shelly <<solar>>
component "Home load" as load <<load>>
component "Solarman SMD1\nGrid smart meter" as smd1 <<meter>>
component "Utility grid" as grid <<grid>>
component "Home Energy Hub\nSF3000 + SFA3600" as hub <<hub>>
component "Indevolt app" as iapp <<out>>

pv -right-> load : <color:#fbbf24>AC</color>
pv .down.> ha : <color:#f59e0b>Modbus PV</color>
ha .down.> shelly : <color:#4ade80>pv_power</color>
shelly .up.> iapp : <color:#4ade80>PV source</color>
hub .up.> iapp : <color:#38bdf8>Battery · native</color>
load -right-> smd1
smd1 -right-> grid : <color:#fbbf24>net</color>
grid -left-> smd1
smd1 .up.> iapp : <color:#a78bfa>Grid source</color>
smd1 .up.> hub : LoRa

note bottom
  App data sources: PV (Shelly on HA) · Battery (native hub) · Grid (SMD1).
  Without a PV meter, SMD1 only sees net import/export — not total solar.
end note

@enduml
